<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saparmurat Niyazov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1940–2006</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Turkmenbashi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saparmurat Niyazov was first secretary of the Communist Party of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> SSR from 1985 and president of independent Turkmenistan from 1991 until his death in 2006. Styling himself Turkmenbashi, &quot;head of the Turkmen&quot;, he built an extreme personality cult, renamed months after himself and his mother, and made his book the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhnama">Ruhnama</a> compulsory reading.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saparmurat-niyazov.jpg" alt="Saparmurat Niyazov" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Danny Gys · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nyyazov_in_February_1998.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
